-- title:
--   Dense q-expansion kernel is a minimal prime (H₁ level)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity $\xi$, and assume some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell_g)}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $X_{H_1}$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and with $\ell_g$ and $M'$ units, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the $j$-invariant. Assume: the conditions [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Point`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma1Pow.html#L10) for $\ell_g$, [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55), and divisibility of [`ModularCurve.inLineMulPoly`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L18) are preserved by Weierstrass variable changes (in the shapes [`ModularCurve.LevelPData.variableChange`](def/ModularCurve_KatzLevelP.html#L84) and [`ModularCurve.kernelVariableChangeDeg`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassLevelComponents.html#L104)); $\mathcal{G}$ is a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras which is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity; $\mathcal{T}$ is a level transport for $\mathcal{G}$ and $q$ which is a section transport; and every variable change, respectively every $A$-algebra map of coefficients, is realised by a graded ring homomorphism of projective-model rings satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`, with the stated irrelevant-ideal condition. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the level moduli datum `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — that is, a ring $B_0$ of finite type over $A$ with a universal point representing the functor of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant equipped with a $\Gamma_0$-type cyclic-kernel polynomial at each prime factor of $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, a Drinfeld level-$q$ basis for $\mathcal{G}$, and the link condition [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Link`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassH1Pow.html#L26). Finally let $\iota : B_0 \to K$ be an $A$-algebra homomorphism whose image is dense in the sense that every $k \in K$ is of the form $\iota(x)/\iota(y)$ with $\iota(y) \ne 0$, and assume $B_0$ is integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by `P₀.j₀`. Then $\ker \iota$ is a minimal prime of $B_0$, i.e. a minimal element of the set of primes containing $(0)$.
--
--   This is the statement that a dense, integral $q$-expansion homomorphism out of the fine moduli ring for the level structure $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ together with Drinfeld level $q$ cuts out a single irreducible component of $\operatorname{Spec} B_0$. It feeds the subsequent counts of minimal primes and the transitivity statements identifying the components of this moduli ring up to $A$-algebra isomorphism.
